WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.706
Homelab build hangs

00:00:01.517 --> 00:00:03.934
four 32 GB V100s

00:00:03.746 --> 00:00:04.335
off

00:00:04.854 --> 00:00:06.174
A homelabber connected

00:00:05.986 --> 00:00:07.283
four used Nvidia

00:00:07.106 --> 00:00:09.547
V100 32 GB cards

00:00:09.382 --> 00:00:10.313
to a Lenovo

00:00:10.125 --> 00:00:12.224
M720q Tiny over

00:00:12.036 --> 00:00:12.908
OCuLink

00:00:13.038 --> 00:00:14.323
using coreboot and

00:00:14.135 --> 00:00:15.089
a solder bridge

00:00:15.252 --> 00:00:17.245
reaching about 285

00:00:17.056 --> 00:00:18.223
tokens per second

00:00:18.035 --> 00:00:19.462
total on Qwen3

00:00:19.273 --> 00:00:19.815
.

00:00:19.639 --> 00:00:21.219
8-27B

00:00:21.742 --> 00:00:23.640
The M720q feeds

00:00:23.452 --> 00:00:24.666
a PCIe switch

00:00:24.478 --> 00:00:25.244
card with a

00:00:25.056 --> 00:00:28.239
24-lane PEX8724 chip

00:00:28.228 --> 00:00:29.124
that fans out

00:00:28.935 --> 00:00:30.208
to four OCuLink

00:00:30.091 --> 00:00:31.164
x4 ports

00:00:31.341 --> 00:00:32.555
giving each GPU

00:00:32.367 --> 00:00:33.982
a PCIe Gen3

00:00:33.841 --> 00:00:34.996
x4 link

00:00:35.534 --> 00:00:36.772
Tom's Hardware puts

00:00:36.584 --> 00:00:37.361
the build at

00:00:37.173 --> 00:00:39.413
about $3,500

00:00:39.661 --> 00:00:40.675
the builder lists

00:00:40.487 --> 00:00:43.824
roughly A$6.5k all-in

00:00:43.895 --> 00:00:45.534
and about 62 dB

00:00:45.345 --> 00:00:46.442
with custom fan

00:00:46.253 --> 00:00:46.925
ducts

00:00:47.454 --> 00:00:48.468
Full story on

00:00:48.279 --> 00:00:49.175
the dashboard
